  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhupendrakumar Bhogilal Shah & vs State Of Gujarat & 2 on 14 October, 2015 Author: J.B.Pardiwala Bench: J.B.Pardiwala R/Scr.A/3077/2014 Order",
    "facts": "All these applications were filed challenging the orders passed by the Adjudicating Officer and the Resident Additional Collector, at a point of time when the Tribunal was not set-up. However, it is pointed out by the learned advocate that vide Government Notification dated 27th July, 2015, issued by the Deputy Secretary to the Government, Health and Family Welfare Department, Gandhinagar, a Presiding Officer has been appointed for the purpose of appeals under Section 70 of the Act, and as per the proceedings mentioned under Rule 3.3 under Chapter III of Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2011. All these applications are not pressed by the learned counsel appearing for the applicants, since the applicants intend to file statutory appeal under Section 70 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 before the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal.",
